# Secrets — never commit. The legacy project had four .env variants in its
# working tree with live credentials; that must not repeat here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build output
/bin/
/tmp/
*.exe
dawa24-store
dawa24-worker

# Local infrastructure state
/.data/

# Coverage
*.out
coverage.html

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# NOTE: *_templ.go is deliberately NOT ignored. The Dockerfile does not run
# `templ generate`, so the generated files must be committed or the container
# build fails on missing symbols.

# Test side effects. The compare and upload handlers write into the served data
# directory, so running the suite leaves a randomly named artefact in the tree
# and it gets committed with whatever change happened to be in flight.
/internal/ui/data/uploads/compare/
/internal/ui/data/orgs/
